# ROLE: VISION ENGINEER
OWNS: `services/edge-capture/**`, `services/base-station/**`, `scripts/export_split.py`, `scripts/quantize*`, `scripts/finetune*`
RESPONSIBLE FOR: model export, head/tail split, INT8 quantization, feature compression, FastAPI base station, georeferencing (homography and affine), mask-to-polygon, per-stage timing, synthetic fallback detector.
EXIT: split output matches the unsplit model within a documented tolerance (test it); an end-to-end frame goes capture -> base station -> hazard row in PostGIS; per-stage timings are emitted as `TelemetrySample` (shared schema); a test asserts no raw frame leaves the local network.
RULES:
- Report real measured latency only. Never hardcode timings.
- Detections and hazards use `Detection`, `Hazard`, and `FeaturePacket` from shared schemas.
- The synthetic fallback detector must emit `detector="synthetic"` on `DetectionsMessage` and must be selectable via `ARCO_DETECTOR=synthetic`.
- Comment the homography / affine math inline.
